## Kata 5

Selected operation: `ExecTnum::neg`.

The existing implementation only proves well-formedness (`r.wf()`).
I added a containment postcondition requiring the result to contain
the two's-complement negation of every concrete value represented by
the input.

Verification failed because `neg` is implemented using `bw_not().add(...)`.
Although `add` already has a containment proof, `bw_not` currently only
guarantees well-formedness. I then attempted to add a containment
postcondition to `bw_not`, which exposed an additional proof obligation
for the all-ones Tnum used by the XOR implementation.

This suggests that proving containment for `neg` requires strengthening
the contracts/proofs of its helper operations first.